taste, but they stand apart in Rhone, Spanish, and Australian wines. Oddly, this wine bar has one of the best full bars in the city. It's the best Sazerac I've ever had (the second best being mine). It's a very friendly neighborhood kind of bar, but very welcoming of all comers. They have special events, like a guest chef who comes in and does small plates on Tuesdays, movie night on Wednesdays, and a band on Saturday. Happy hour every night is a great deal."},{"business_id":"Pbv4IH4OIzY-9Zv1JaKPWw","review_id":"A0yhYiBCEvWud02kfPe6YA","date":"2011-10-25T04:42:34","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9233942031860352,"text_excerpt":"Perfect place for a chill night at a wine bar that isn't packed. I came on a Friday and there was a live band. Every seat was taken but there weren't many people standing around which is nice. I don't like places where you have to rub up against people, ew germs and sexual harassment! Anyways, the wine and drinks are great and the bartenders were nice and attentive."}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
